{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KXBUrKKNVYvJttv14FW8hm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go from formal specifications (SRDs), verified by differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It is a stress test for the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/<name>/` holds per-utility implementations with differential tests. `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/format/`, `pkg/testutils/`, `pkg/hashutil/`, `pkg/sizeparse/`, `pkg/encutil/` provide shared infrastructure. SRDs under `docs/specs/` are the source of truth.\n\n**Current state**: 33 releases (00.0–15.0) are spec-complete. Many utilities across releases are implemented, but gaps remain. The most recently completed work is `cmd/mv` R1.1–R2.4 (tasks 5396–5397).\n\n**Earliest incomplete release with ready requirements**: rel07.1 — `srd057-mv` has R3.1–R3.3 and R4.1–R4.4 ready; `srd058-rm` has R1.1–R4.4 all ready.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **cmd/mv (srd057)** — Partially implemented (R1–R2 done). R3.1–R3.3 and R4.1–R4.4 remain. Finishing mv first since work is in progress.\n2. **cmd/rm (srd058)** — Not started. New package needs a contract task before implementation. 16 ready requirements; only R1.1–R1.4 fit this batch.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\n```\nTask 0: srd057-mv R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1) → total = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd057-mv R4.1 (w=1), R4.2 (w=1), R4.3 (w=1), R4.4 (w=1) → total = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: contract (no weighted requirements) ✓\nTask 3: srd058-rm R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1) → total = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/mv: srd057 R3.1-R3.3\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd057-mv.yaml (R3.1-R3.3 requirements and acceptance criteria)\n      - cmd/mv/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R2.4)\n      - cmd/mv/mv_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mv/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R3.1-R3.3 functionality to existing mv implementation\n      - path: cmd/mv/mv_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases covering R3.1-R3.3\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd057-mv requirement R3.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd057-mv requirement R3.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd057-mv requirement R3.3 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Modify the existing cmd/mv/main.go -- do not rewrite or restructure code from R1.1-R2.4\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use testutils.RunDiffTests with gmv reference binary for all new test cases\n      - id: D3\n        text: Call exec.LookPath(\"gmv\") and t.Skip if reference binary is not found\n      - id: D4\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in test environment variables for deterministic comparison\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/mv/ succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/mv/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/mv/... -count=1 passes, including new R3.1-R3.3 test cases\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: All R3.1-R3.3 requirements from srd057-mv are implemented and tested\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Existing tests for R1.1-R2.4 continue to pass without modification\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/mv: srd057 R4.1-R4.4\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd057-mv.yaml (R4.1-R4.4 requirements and acce